WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.480
You click a work link.

2
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:03.800
And it opens in your personal browser,

3
00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:05.430
where you're not even signed in.

4
00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:07.160
Junction fixes that.

5
00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:09.600
It becomes your Mac's default browser,

6
00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:11.800
and sends every link where it belongs.

7
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.910
A Jira ticket goes to Chrome,

8
00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.060
in your work profile.

9
00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:18.610
A Zoom invite skips the browser, and opens the Zoom app.

10
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.850
Reddit stays in Firefox.

11
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:22.760
It's all just a list of rules.

12
00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:26.170
Match a domain, a wildcard, or the app you clicked in.

13
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:27.750
First match wins.

14
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:29.800
Wondering where a link will go?

15
00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.270
Paste it into the tester.

16
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.660
Junction strips the tracking junk,

17
00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:35.800
and shows you the rule that catches it.

18
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:36.960
Can't decide?

19
00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:40.700
Hold Option when you click, and pick a browser, right at your cursor.

20
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:43.360
Nineteen built-in deep links

21
00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.400
open Slack, Figma, Spotify and more,

22
00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:46.740
straight in their apps.

23
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.620
Your rules live in a JSON file you own,

24
00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.740
switch on and off from the menu bar,

25
00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.250
and sync across your Macs with iCloud.

26
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:55.310
Junction.

27
00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:57.680
Free, open source, zero telemetry.

28
00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:59.590
Every link, in the right place.
